<title>JAPAN: Japan Apr-Jun GDP deflator first rise in two years.</title>
<headline>Japan Apr-Jun GDP deflator first rise in two years.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's inflation, measured by the gross domestic product (GDP) deflator, rose 0.3 percent in the April-June quarter from the same quarter a year earlier, the government's Economic Planning Agency said on Friday.</p>
<p>It was the first year-on-year increase in the deflator in two years, the agency said in a statement. In the January-March period, the GDP deflator fell 0.1 percent year-on-year.</p>
</text>
